    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 1.5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hine hwa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.18"/> forstonde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.19"/>, forgilde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.7-2"/> hine be his were, swa þam cyninge swa ðam ðe hit mid ryhte togebyrige; ⁊ ælc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.20"/> man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.5"/> ðara ðe þær midstande gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.8-2"/> ðam cyninge CXX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.5" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.8"/> hwa hine forstande, forgylde hine be his were, swa ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.7"/> cynge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.21"/> swa ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.7"/> ðe hit togebyrige; ⁊ ælc man ðara ðe ðær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.22"/> midstande gesylle hundtwelftig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.23"/> scill' to wite ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.7"/> cynge.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.21"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.5" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>Ond gif hine hwa foran forstande, forgylde hine be his were, swa ðæm cyning<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.3"/> swa þæm þe hit togebyrige; ⁊ ælc þara þe þær midstande geselle CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.5-2"/> scill' to wite þam cyninge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="151" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis obstabit, persoluat se wera sua, sic regi sic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.21-2"/> ei, cui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.10"/> pertinet (cuius rectum erit); et omnis, qui cum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.10"/> eo stabit (coadiuuabit), emendet CXX sol. wyte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.22-2"/> regi.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.23-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="1.5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="128" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ gif hine hwa forstonde<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_1-5.attnote.fn.4"/>, forgilde hine be his were, swa þam cyninge swa ðam ðe hit mid ryhte togebyrige; ⁊ ælc man ðara ðe þær midstande gesylle ðam cyninge CXX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="151" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn jemand (vorweg<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.1"/> <hi rend="italic">So</hi>) für ihn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.2"/> [hiergegen] eintritt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.3"/>, so bezahle er ihn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.4"/> durch dessen Wergeld entweder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.5"/> dem König oder wem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.6"/> es gesetzlich zusteht; und jedermann, welcher da [zur Widersetzlichkeit] beisteht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.7"/>, gebe dem König 120 Schilling<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.8"/> als Strafgeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone (beforehand, So) intervenes for him [against this], let him pay for him with his wergild either to the king or to whomever it lawfully belongs; and everyone who stands by [in the resistance] there is to give the king 120 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="129" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone defends him, he shall pay for him to the amount of his<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_1-5.attnote.n.1"/> wergeld, either to the king or to him<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_1-5.attnote.n.2"/> to whom it is legally due, and everyone who renders him assistance shall pay a fine of 120 shillings to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone defends him, he is to pay for him with his wergild, whether to the king or to him to whom it rightly belongs; and everyone of those who supported him is to pay 120 shillings to the king as a fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIAs_1-3">VI As 1.3</ref>; <ref target="clause:IAtr_4-2">I Atr 4.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="207"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_30-3b">II Cn 30.3b</ref> <quote>These are therefore responsible for their dependents' behaviour, by which token (b cf. l) they're entitled to the criminal's wergeld</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="207"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_30-6">II Cn 30.6</ref> <quote>These are therefore responsible for their dependents' behaviour, by which token (b cf. l) they're entitled to the criminal's wergeld</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyng <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyng Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þære <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þære Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">CXX <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">CXX Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Rasur von vier Buchst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by an erasure of four letters</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> -stande</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -stande</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o. h. be þ[am <hi rend="italic">verschnitten</hi>] gel. <hi rend="italic">am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o. h. be þ[am cropped] gel. in the margin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.21-2" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sic — regi <hi rend="italic">überspringt MHkBr, wo nur</hi> wyte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic — regi skipped by MHkBr, which have only wyte</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond;</hi> (<hi rend="italic">eingeklammertes</hi>) <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">before the bracket Lond; (the bracketed words) the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.22-2" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> r. w. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Lond; r. w. the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.23-2" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">regis <hi rend="italic">KT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">regis KT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">CXX <hi rend="italic">bis</hi> cyninge <hi rend="italic">doppelt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">CXX to cyninge written twice</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So's <hi rend="italic">foran</hi> wird gegen hb authentisch sein; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> VI 1, 4 <hi rend="italic">forene,</hi> wo dies zitiert wird; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb: foran, forene</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So's <hi rend="italic">foran</hi> is likely to be authentic as against hb; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> VI 1, 4 <hi rend="italic">forene,</hi> where this is cited; see <hi rend="italic">Wb: foran, forene</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q übersieht <hi rend="italic">hine</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q overlooks <hi rend="italic">hine</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q ungenau, doch sinnentsprechend: ‘widersteht’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q inexact, but true to the sense: ‘resists’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘löse sich durch sein (des Begünstigers) Wergeld’ Q, grammatisch möglich und nicht ohne Parallele, aber hier laut 1, 1; 4. 2, 2 falsch, trotz der späteren Strenge V Pro 3. VI 1, 4, die Begünstigung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2—5. 7) mit Tod bedroht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘let him redeem himself by his (the abettor's) wergild’ Q, grammatically possible and not without parallel, but wrong here according to 1, 1; 4. 2, 2, despite the later severity of V Pro 3. VI 1, 4, which threatens abetting (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2—5. 7) with death</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘sowohl . . als auch’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘both . . and’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Neben dem Könige ist nicht der Staatsbeamte, sondern eine private Macht zu denken, Adel oder Prälat. Doch braucht As hier nicht Gerichtsbarkeit (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 11 b) zu meinen, sondern nur Strafgeldempfang</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Alongside the king one should think not of the state official but of a private power, a noble or a prelate. As need not, however, mean jurisdiction here (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 11 b), but only the receipt of fines</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">mid</hi> kann auch Adverb sein; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> 146 Sp. 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">mid</hi> can also be an adverb; see <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> 146 col. 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Ungehorsam 23</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Ungehorsam 23</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e</hi>. the thief’s wergeld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">According to Liebermann, some private authority (either nobleman or prelate) who is entitled to receive fines.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_1-5.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope></bibl><label>forstonde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">foran forstande</hi>. So.</seg></note>
      </div>
